@startuml
title LegacyVault Flow 5 - Legal Verification

actor "Digital Executor / Trustee" as Executor
actor "Legal Verifier" as Verifier
participant "LegacyVault Web UI" as UI
participant "LegalVerificationCaseController" as Controller
participant "LegalVerificationService" as Service
participant "ActivationGateway\n(Flow 4 adapter pending)" as Activation
participant "DocumentStorage\n(private storage adapter pending)" as Storage
database "MySQL" as DB

note over Executor,DB
Only an authenticated, authorized user may act. The local scaffold expects
a trusted servlet principal and DIGITAL_EXECUTOR / LEGAL_VERIFIER roles.
The default Flow 4 and storage adapters return 503 until connected.
Flow 5 records an internal review outcome; it does not decide inheritance
rights, send notifications, decrypt assets, or invoke Flow 6.
end note

Executor -> UI: Start verification for an eligible activation
UI -> Controller: POST /api/legal-verification-cases {activationId}
Controller -> Service: createDraft(principal, activationId)
Service -> Activation: requireExecutorAssignment(activationId, executorId)
alt Flow 4 adapter not configured
  Activation --> Service: 503 Integration not configured
  Service --> Controller: Error response
  Controller --> UI: 503 Service Unavailable
else activation exists and executor is assigned
  Activation --> Service: Assignment confirmed
  Service -> DB: Save DRAFT case + CASE_CREATED event
  DB --> Service: caseId
  Service --> Controller: Case response
  Controller --> UI: 201 Created
end

loop Upload death certificate and applicable supporting evidence
  Executor -> UI: Choose document type and file
  UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/documents (multipart)
  Controller -> Service: uploadDocument(principal, caseId, file)
  Service -> Service: Check owner, case state, size, and file signature
  alt private storage adapter not configured
    Service -> Storage: store(documentId, bytes)
    Storage --> Service: 503 Integration not configured
    Service --> Controller: Error response
    Controller --> UI: 503 Service Unavailable
  else private encrypted storage configured
    Service -> Storage: Store bytes privately
    Storage --> Service: storageKey + SHA-256
    Service -> DB: Save metadata + DOCUMENT_UPLOADED event
    DB --> Service: Saved
    Service --> Controller: Document metadata only
    Controller --> UI: 201 Created
  end
end

Executor -> UI: Submit verification request
UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/submit
Controller -> Service: submit(principal, caseId)
Service -> DB: Check for DEATH_CERTIFICATE metadata
alt Required evidence missing
  Service --> Controller: 422 REQUIRED_EVIDENCE_MISSING
  Controller --> UI: Show validation issue
else Required evidence present
  Service -> DB: DRAFT/NEEDS_INFORMATION to SUBMITTED + event
  DB --> Service: Saved
  Service --> Controller: Updated case
  Controller --> UI: 200 OK
end

Verifier -> UI: Open review queue
UI -> Controller: GET /api/legal-verification-cases?status=SUBMITTED
Controller -> Service: listCases(principal)
Service -> DB: Find unassigned SUBMITTED + cases assigned to this reviewer
DB --> Service: Scoped case summaries
Service --> Controller: Queue response
Controller --> UI: 200 OK

Verifier -> UI: Claim submitted case
UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/start-review
Controller -> Service: startReview(principal, caseId)
Service -> DB: Assign reviewer; SUBMITTED to IN_REVIEW + event
DB --> Service: Updated case
Service --> Controller: Case response
Controller --> UI: 200 OK

Verifier -> UI: Inspect an evidence document
UI -> Controller: GET /{caseId}/documents/{documentId}/content
Controller -> Service: authorizeAndRead(principal, caseId, documentId)
Service -> DB: Check case, reviewer assignment, and document metadata
DB --> Service: Authorized storage key
Service -> Storage: read(private storage key)
Storage --> Service: File bytes
Service --> Controller: Authorized file content
Controller --> UI: File response

alt More information is needed
  Verifier -> UI: Enter required information and reason
  UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/request-information
  Controller -> Service: requestInformation(principal, caseId, reason)
  Service -> DB: IN_REVIEW to NEEDS_INFORMATION + event
  DB --> Service: Saved
  Service --> Controller: Updated case
  Controller --> UI: 200 OK
  note over Executor,UI
  No notification integration is wired yet; the executor sees the change
  by refreshing/polling the case.
  end note
  Executor -> UI: Upload missing evidence and resubmit
  UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/documents, then /{caseId}/submit
  Controller -> Service: Upload and resubmit as authenticated executor
  Service -> DB: Save document metadata, then NEEDS_INFORMATION to SUBMITTED
else Review is complete
  Verifier -> UI: Record APPROVED or REJECTED with reason
  UI -> Controller: POST /{caseId}/decision
  Controller -> Service: decide(principal, caseId, outcome, reason)
  Service -> Service: Check role, assigned reviewer, and state
  Service -> DB: Save final status + decision event
  DB --> Service: Saved
  Service --> Controller: Decision response
  Controller --> UI: 200 OK
  note over Service,DB
  APPROVED is only a Flow 5 outcome. Flow 6 must separately verify identity,
  asset assignment, and release conditions. No handover call occurs here.
  end note
end

@enduml
